1. P2 — Complete the new IPv6 authority integration in onboarding. `LocalFactoryAccess.ts:18` adds `[::1]`, but `FactoryServer.ts:588` and `:618` duplicate IPv4-only hostname lists. This is possible Duplicated Code with a confirmed consequential mismatch against the maintained IPv6/local-onboarding contract (`docs/PRODUCT_CONTRACTS.md`). A real socket request to `http://[::1]:37451` returns authenticated local status, omits onboarding from `/api/config`, and returns 409 for `/api/onboarding` and project-save POST (“Complete machine setup at the localhost address”). IPv4/localhost controls return onboarding and 200. Fresh IPv6 clients therefore skip guided setup and cannot configure a project. Apply the shared validated local-authority classification consistently to both onboarding checks, retaining remote restrictions. Reproducer uses the actual server/listeners and a stub onboarding service to isolate authority gating: `/tmp/pr99-standards-extra/onboarding.test.ts`; raw output: `/tmp/pr99-standards-extra/result.log`. Run from the snapshot’s `packages/edge-worker`: `./node_modules/.bin/vitest run --config /tmp/pr99-standards-extra/config.mts --reporter=verbose`.

2. P2 — Remove contradictory localhost passkey guidance. The changed `Workflow.ts:291` capability string says local startup needs no enrollment/login, then still says “The Factory dashboard requires passkey sessions on every address, including localhost” and that an empty store shows first-passkey setup. This contradicts the maintained Dashboard access contract and the same exported instruction. `EdgeWorker.ts:8483`, `PromptBuilder.ts:688`, Slack and Zulip inject it into live agent prompts, giving agents obsolete setup/recovery instructions. Replace those retained sentences with explicit local/remote behavior. Reproduce: `bun /tmp/pr99-standards-extra/prompt.ts`; output: `/tmp/pr99-standards-extra/prompt.log`.

